<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janusz I of Warsaw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1346–<a href="/years/1429">1429</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Janusz the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Janusz I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> (c. 1346–1429), also called Janusz the Elder, was a Piast duke who ruled the northern and eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> from 1374. He made Warsaw his main residence, laying the foundations of its later role as the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. A loyal ally of Poland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, he fought against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grunwald">Battle of Grunwald</a> in 1410.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janusz-i-of-warsaw.jpg" alt="Janusz I of Warsaw" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janusz_I_Starszy_seal_1376.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
